  "goodToKnow": "Worin means in what or in which. It's a wo-compound, used for questions about things, not people: Worin liegt der Vorteil? (wherein lies the advantage?). Common with bestehen in: Worin besteht der Unterschied? It can also introduce a relative clause: das Haus, worin ich wohnte, though in dem is more usual today. Other wo-compounds: woran, worauf, worüber, wovon, womit."
